# D1 needs no connection string: the binding is declared in wrangler.json and
# injected by the Workers runtime. The CLI reads .wrangler/state by default.
# For deliberate remote administration only, set these in your shell:
# HEYO_D1_REMOTE=1
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=...
# CLOUDFLARE_D1_DATABASE_ID=...
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=...   # D1 Edit; never commit this token
